        <type>bool</type>
        <definition>bool ProfileReport::toFile</definition>
        <argsstring>(const juce::ValueTree &amp;profiles, const juce::NamedValueSet &amp;properties, const juce::File &amp;outputFile)</argsstring>
        <name>toFile</name>
        <qualifiedname>ProfileReport::toFile</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>const juce::ValueTree &amp;</type>
          <declname>profiles</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const juce::NamedValueSet &amp;</type>
          <declname>properties</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const juce::File &amp;</type>
          <declname>outputFile</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Writes the report of <computeroutput>profiles</computeroutput> to <computeroutput>outputFile</computeroutput>. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The function builds the report document from <computeroutput>profiles</computeroutput> and adds the charts of each profile table. It writes the document through <computeroutput>jam::MarkdownWriter</computeroutput>, which creates the parent folder of <computeroutput>outputFile</computeroutput>. It adds <computeroutput>properties</computeroutput> as the front matter of the document.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>profiles</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Tree of the profile tables that <ref refid="class_benchmark_1ac2758e9667d09cca4fa1c7d0845c7413" kindref="member">Benchmark::getProfiles()</ref> returns. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>properties</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The front matter properties of the report. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>outputFile</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>File that receives the report. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><computeroutput>true</computeroutput> when the write succeeds, or <computeroutput>false</computeroutput> when it fails. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
